WEBVTT

00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:16.180
Hey, Al!

00:00:16.930 --> 00:00:18.760
Is that an Echo Device?

00:00:19.430 --> 00:00:20.640
That's right!

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:23.690
So, the power of songs is making you fly?

00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:28.230
Do you remember how Rin made
the carriage fly with the Song of Wind?

00:00:28.310 --> 00:00:29.820
I thought if I used that,

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:32.190
with the current level
of scientific technology--

00:00:40.490 --> 00:00:41.450
Ouch.

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:43.960
My head hurts.

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:47.540
It can't be helped.
It's only meant for one person.

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:49.960
That was a pretty bad fall.

00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:52.760
You could have broken something.

00:00:53.090 --> 00:00:55.260
You don't have to point that out.

00:00:57.640 --> 00:00:59.800
Huh? What's going on?!

00:00:59.890 --> 00:01:02.020
Hey, wait. That's mine, right?

00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:03.480
When did you--?

00:01:04.850 --> 00:01:07.850
Hey, why are you laughing?!
I don't get it!

00:01:07.940 --> 00:01:09.770
Ah. You're so loud!

00:01:09.860 --> 00:01:11.480
You're so loud, Al.

00:01:11.570 --> 00:01:14.030
Hey! I came to save you!

00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:18.450
I don't get what you're trying to do!

00:01:19.280 --> 00:01:20.620
-You know...
<i>-Help me.</i>

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:23.120
your actions are
scientifically impossible!

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:25.120
<i>Help me. Help me. Help me.</i>

00:01:25.210 --> 00:01:27.210
<i>Help me. Help me. Help me.</i>

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:29.830
<i>Help me.</i>

00:03:06.600 --> 00:03:08.220
The Song of Silence

00:03:08.850 --> 00:03:11.230
Sorry. We're going to camp here tonight.

00:03:12.150 --> 00:03:13.810
We still have a long way to go.

00:03:14.270 --> 00:03:17.280
By the way, what's a knight
from the Leobolt family doing

00:03:17.360 --> 00:03:19.610
leading a group of mercenaries?

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:21.740
Yeah.

00:03:22.240 --> 00:03:25.490
I thought you were a kidnapper
when you saved us.

00:03:25.580 --> 00:03:28.040
Hey. That's not nice.

00:03:28.700 --> 00:03:29.620
That's Berow.

00:03:30.410 --> 00:03:32.000
And that guy's Snore.

00:03:32.460 --> 00:03:33.880
They used to be mercenaries.

00:03:34.210 --> 00:03:37.630
But now they're rebelling
against the Capital Army like me.

00:03:38.210 --> 00:03:39.960
Our rules are simple.

00:03:40.590 --> 00:03:42.340
We follow the strongest guy.

00:03:42.930 --> 00:03:45.760
Even if he's a rich kid from the Capital.

00:03:46.890 --> 00:03:51.770
Well, we fell in love with his strength.
Right, Berow?

00:03:52.270 --> 00:03:54.650
I know how you feel.

00:03:54.730 --> 00:03:56.860
I understand
why you fell in love with him.

00:03:57.770 --> 00:03:58.900
Okay, okay.

00:04:00.280 --> 00:04:02.610
But I wasn't able to defeat Bazra...

00:04:03.490 --> 00:04:05.370
or save Finis.

00:04:09.490 --> 00:04:10.750
Leader! It's an airship!

00:04:12.910 --> 00:04:14.790
Stay down! Try not to move!

00:04:21.340 --> 00:04:24.260
Bazra, you bastard.
He's going to the Capital.

00:04:24.840 --> 00:04:26.890
That's the Master's flying ship.

00:04:28.300 --> 00:04:29.970
We have to go by land.

00:04:30.430 --> 00:04:34.440
We'll rest today and head
for Dr. Weissen's laboratory tomorrow.

00:04:38.060 --> 00:04:38.900
<i>Finis...</i>

00:04:44.030 --> 00:04:45.820
There was some trouble,

00:04:46.530 --> 00:04:48.780
but the Star Song Festival will
soon begin.

00:04:49.490 --> 00:04:52.250
Everything's ready
for the Song of Mortality, right?

00:04:53.160 --> 00:04:56.790
If the Court Orchestra has
the Graphic notation, everything is set.

00:04:57.380 --> 00:04:59.540
All that's left to do is sing.

00:05:00.670 --> 00:05:02.880
What are you thinking?

00:05:05.470 --> 00:05:09.100
The Song of Mortality is
an important weapon to me.

00:05:09.850 --> 00:05:12.180
But what does it mean to you?

00:05:12.640 --> 00:05:14.600
I'm sure they'll come again.

00:05:15.230 --> 00:05:18.440
I'm not going to let them interfere
with the song.

00:05:19.980 --> 00:05:23.320
I'm the one who's going to attack them
in the Capital.

00:05:23.860 --> 00:05:25.530
I won't let them interfere.

00:05:30.280 --> 00:05:32.910
Even though you lost the Symphony Killer?

00:05:34.160 --> 00:05:35.960
You're awfully chatty today.

00:05:36.620 --> 00:05:37.870
What happened?

00:05:40.250 --> 00:05:41.250
Don't worry.

00:05:41.790 --> 00:05:46.220
The one we deployed in Ash City was
just a prototype made by Dr. Weissen.

00:05:48.590 --> 00:05:50.720
<i>Wait for us, Finis!</i>

00:05:53.560 --> 00:05:55.890
Her voice won't go away.

00:06:12.580 --> 00:06:15.120
The Curse of Immortality, huh?

00:06:15.790 --> 00:06:19.080
But that's scientifically impossible!

00:06:19.500 --> 00:06:23.340
But everything Rin said is true.

00:06:24.550 --> 00:06:27.760
Even things from the past
that no one else knows about except me.

00:06:29.760 --> 00:06:33.550
But... why was Rin the only one
who could replay the songs

00:06:33.640 --> 00:06:36.520
from the past
that floated around in the air?

00:06:38.020 --> 00:06:40.350
That's because I--

00:06:42.440 --> 00:06:44.270
Anyway, we have to stop Finis.

00:06:44.360 --> 00:06:45.570
Stop her?

00:06:46.280 --> 00:06:49.070
What in the world is she trying to do?

00:06:49.900 --> 00:06:53.370
She's planning to sing
the Song of Mortality again.

00:06:55.080 --> 00:06:58.700
She's trying to recreate
the ancient legend of the songstress...

00:06:59.500 --> 00:07:01.540
where a meteor destroys the continent.

00:07:03.040 --> 00:07:03.960
That's not it.

00:07:07.920 --> 00:07:09.050
Finis is...

00:07:09.880 --> 00:07:11.760
trying to make that huge star fall...

00:07:13.140 --> 00:07:15.680
and destroy the entire world.

00:07:19.770 --> 00:07:22.690
I just got back. Why did you summon me?

00:07:23.190 --> 00:07:24.770
General Bazra.

00:07:25.150 --> 00:07:28.110
I know you're in charge
of the Capital Army,

00:07:28.400 --> 00:07:30.400
but you go off on your own too much.

00:07:30.490 --> 00:07:32.110
The king is right!

00:07:32.490 --> 00:07:35.950
Do you have any idea
how much money you've spent?

00:07:36.330 --> 00:07:38.490
Making another one of those huge things...

00:07:38.910 --> 00:07:40.410
If money is what it takes,

00:07:40.710 --> 00:07:43.960
then all you have to do is raise taxes.

00:07:44.040 --> 00:07:46.090
The people aren't going to stay quiet!

00:07:46.170 --> 00:07:49.550
Then you just have
to make them stay quiet.

00:07:52.470 --> 00:07:54.300
It's nothing to worry about.

00:07:54.970 --> 00:07:59.390
The Kingdom of Golt will soon
rule the world.

00:08:05.190 --> 00:08:07.570
You worthless royal scum...

00:08:09.150 --> 00:08:11.070
Is the new model ready?

00:08:11.150 --> 00:08:13.490
Yes, sir. We're almost ready.

00:08:13.570 --> 00:08:16.740
Don't let anyone interfere
with the Song of Mortality.

00:08:17.280 --> 00:08:20.040
Leobolt will definitely show up.

00:08:20.750 --> 00:08:22.580
Tighten security at the castle gate.

00:08:22.960 --> 00:08:23.790
Yes, sir!

00:08:26.830 --> 00:08:29.880
<i>Bazra's goal is to rule</i>
<i>the entire continent.</i>

00:08:29.960 --> 00:08:34.340
Finis and her power of songs are
the ace up his sleeve.

00:08:34.760 --> 00:08:36.720
And from Finis's point of view,

00:08:36.800 --> 00:08:39.850
helping Bazra will help her get
what she wants.

00:08:40.390 --> 00:08:43.180
They have a common interest.
Finis kept waiting...

00:08:43.770 --> 00:08:46.480
until the day
on which the star is closest to us.

00:08:46.940 --> 00:08:47.810
In other words,

00:08:47.900 --> 00:08:50.190
<i>the Star Song Festival</i>
<i>and the Court Orchestra</i>

00:08:50.270 --> 00:08:52.030
<i>maximize the power of songs,</i>

00:08:52.530 --> 00:08:54.900
<i>and she's been waiting</i>
<i>for the day she has both.</i>

00:08:55.490 --> 00:08:59.030
If you sing to the stars,
your wishes will come true, huh?

00:08:59.580 --> 00:09:04.620
It was actually Finis's wish,
who's been through eternity.

00:09:05.370 --> 00:09:07.710
I wonder if she's a bad person.

00:09:08.210 --> 00:09:09.340
That's not true.

00:09:10.340 --> 00:09:13.130
I heard Finis's voice at the end.

00:09:13.710 --> 00:09:15.260
She was saying:

00:09:16.380 --> 00:09:17.550
"Help me."

00:09:17.930 --> 00:09:18.970
"Help me"?

00:09:19.640 --> 00:09:23.350
I don't think she really wants
to sing the Song of Mortality.

00:09:24.100 --> 00:09:25.560
She wants us to help her.

00:09:26.190 --> 00:09:27.020
So...

00:09:28.810 --> 00:09:29.900
<i>we have to help her.</i>

00:09:33.150 --> 00:09:35.780
<i>I heard your voice!</i>

00:09:36.610 --> 00:09:39.490
<i>I'm coming to save you, no matter what!</i>

00:09:43.790 --> 00:09:44.700
Who are you?

00:09:45.830 --> 00:09:47.120
You're coming to save me?

00:09:50.080 --> 00:09:51.920
I won't let you get in the way.

00:09:58.720 --> 00:09:59.550
Rin...

00:10:00.600 --> 00:10:03.850
-You're worried about her, aren't you?
-Mr. Leobolt.

00:10:04.850 --> 00:10:07.230
Immortality... The power of songs...

00:10:07.940 --> 00:10:10.810
There are things happening
that we can't understand.

00:10:12.820 --> 00:10:16.400
The only one who understands is
that little girl.

00:10:17.820 --> 00:10:19.240
Why does she...

00:10:20.110 --> 00:10:22.200
always care about others so much?

00:10:23.450 --> 00:10:25.950
She sings for others
with everything she's got.

00:10:27.580 --> 00:10:29.330
She wanted to sing in the Capital.

00:10:30.370 --> 00:10:31.920
That was all...

00:10:33.210 --> 00:10:34.550
That's all that Rin...

00:10:39.090 --> 00:10:41.890
Five years ago, when I was in the Capital,

00:10:42.430 --> 00:10:43.850
I met a woman.

00:10:50.390 --> 00:10:52.730
<i>I'll never forget... that day.</i>

00:10:55.520 --> 00:10:56.820
<i>There was one noblewoman</i>

00:10:57.440 --> 00:10:59.360
<i>in the Court Orchestra.</i>

00:11:00.490 --> 00:11:02.660
<i>I couldn't see her face</i>
<i>because of her mask.</i>

00:11:02.740 --> 00:11:04.780
<i>But she played beautiful music.</i>

00:11:05.490 --> 00:11:07.410
<i>I immediately fell in love with her.</i>

00:11:09.620 --> 00:11:12.540
-You understand, right?
-What are you saying?

00:11:12.920 --> 00:11:15.000
I don't understand...

00:11:15.670 --> 00:11:19.920
But... she disappeared before long.

00:11:21.510 --> 00:11:22.840
You heard about it, right?

00:11:23.390 --> 00:11:26.760
How the first princess
of the Kingdom of Golt disappeared.

00:11:27.890 --> 00:11:29.680
-Was it--?
-Yes.

00:11:30.600 --> 00:11:34.230
The woman I fell in love with was
the princess of the Kingdom of Golt,

00:11:34.310 --> 00:11:35.480
Alea Golt.

00:11:36.020 --> 00:11:37.070
The princess...

00:11:37.940 --> 00:11:39.280
I remember now.

00:11:39.360 --> 00:11:43.990
She abandoned the Court Orchestra
and vanished without a trace.

00:11:44.570 --> 00:11:47.450
It's unlikely that she survived the war.

00:11:48.410 --> 00:11:50.620
I couldn't find the woman I love.

00:11:51.460 --> 00:11:53.750
I was so helpless. It frustrated me.

00:11:54.960 --> 00:11:56.040
Mr. Leobolt...

00:11:57.000 --> 00:11:57.880
So...

00:11:58.880 --> 00:12:00.210
I understand how you feel.

00:12:03.260 --> 00:12:06.680
I knew that Talgia found a baby.

00:12:07.300 --> 00:12:09.470
But I never imagined
that baby was you, Rin.

00:12:11.730 --> 00:12:13.600
He was an emotional fellow.

00:12:14.310 --> 00:12:16.400
He was my best friend.

00:12:17.400 --> 00:12:18.940
I kind of figured.

00:12:21.650 --> 00:12:22.490
Rin.

00:12:25.280 --> 00:12:27.910
Is there something
you haven't told me yet?

00:12:31.000 --> 00:12:33.290
<i>Rin's bad at peeling apples.</i>

00:12:34.830 --> 00:12:36.210
She likes to eat them,

00:12:36.710 --> 00:12:38.840
but she doesn't like the peel.

00:12:39.500 --> 00:12:41.760
She wanted to eat peeled apples.

00:12:42.670 --> 00:12:44.300
She's always being selfish.

00:12:48.760 --> 00:12:51.180
I wanted to surprise her.

00:12:52.390 --> 00:12:54.140
I wanted to see her happy.

00:12:55.190 --> 00:12:57.610
That's why I was always making things.

00:12:59.320 --> 00:13:02.530
Not because I wanted
to become a famous scientist,

00:13:03.490 --> 00:13:08.070
or to make things
that help other people like the Master.

00:13:08.820 --> 00:13:11.040
I-- I--

00:13:15.500 --> 00:13:17.420
I haven't given up, Al.

00:13:19.210 --> 00:13:20.840
The princess is alive somewhere.

00:13:21.500 --> 00:13:23.590
I'll find her, no matter what.

00:13:24.420 --> 00:13:25.720
Mr. Leobolt...

00:13:26.340 --> 00:13:29.760
I'm going to restore the Capital
and bring back the princess.

00:13:30.720 --> 00:13:31.720
Then...

00:13:32.350 --> 00:13:34.180
I'm going to tell her how I feel.

00:13:36.980 --> 00:13:40.190
I'm going to do whatever I can for her.

00:13:41.070 --> 00:13:42.570
That's what a man would do.

00:13:46.280 --> 00:13:48.490
I'm sure she'll eat it with a smile.

00:13:50.200 --> 00:13:51.030
Thank you.

00:13:53.450 --> 00:13:55.450
Is that true?!

00:14:00.250 --> 00:14:01.130
Rin...

00:14:02.380 --> 00:14:03.380
You're...

00:14:06.720 --> 00:14:08.470
Let's go to the Capital!

00:14:10.090 --> 00:14:11.760
Huh? Ahem.

00:14:12.510 --> 00:14:14.520
Let's go to the Capital!

00:14:14.600 --> 00:14:16.310
Don't worry. We heard you.

00:14:16.390 --> 00:14:18.810
Then please say something!

00:14:18.890 --> 00:14:20.480
You look happy today.

00:14:20.560 --> 00:14:21.810
Huh? What do you mean?

00:14:22.400 --> 00:14:24.940
What were you talking about
with Mr. Leobolt?

00:14:25.230 --> 00:14:27.530
That's a secret between us men.

00:14:27.610 --> 00:14:29.570
-You were crying, weren't you?
-What?!

00:14:29.660 --> 00:14:32.830
-Your eyes are puffy.
-You're right. Crybaby.

00:14:33.160 --> 00:14:34.080
Cryglasses.

00:14:34.870 --> 00:14:37.910
Be quiet! What do you mean, "cryglasses"?!

00:14:41.080 --> 00:14:43.670
According to the Master,
this Graphic notation

00:14:43.750 --> 00:14:46.010
is the Song of Mortality by Finis.

00:14:46.550 --> 00:14:48.420
My grandfather had it.

00:14:49.260 --> 00:14:52.800
We have to stop Finis's plan,
no matter what.

00:14:53.680 --> 00:14:54.680
Al...

00:15:01.350 --> 00:15:02.270
Well,

00:15:02.730 --> 00:15:04.110
what should we do?

00:15:05.150 --> 00:15:07.150
Before they sing the Song of Mortality,

00:15:07.610 --> 00:15:09.530
I'm going to sing the Song of Healing.

00:15:10.110 --> 00:15:12.200
That's what the Song of Healing is for.

00:15:14.660 --> 00:15:16.740
So... only I...

00:15:17.040 --> 00:15:19.750
Rin's Orchestra finally makes its debut
in the Capital.

00:15:20.920 --> 00:15:23.790
-A rising star appears.
-Appears.

00:15:24.210 --> 00:15:26.340
To sing in the Capital with an orchestra,

00:15:27.090 --> 00:15:28.460
that was your dream, right?

00:15:29.130 --> 00:15:31.090
My dream...

00:15:31.510 --> 00:15:32.720
Let's make it come true!

00:15:38.310 --> 00:15:39.220
Al...

00:15:40.730 --> 00:15:41.810
All right!

00:15:41.890 --> 00:15:44.650
-I have nothing more to say. Al!
-Yes!

00:15:45.060 --> 00:15:47.270
It's time to debut the thing
we talked about.

00:15:51.280 --> 00:15:53.200
Open the gate!

00:16:03.080 --> 00:16:04.750
Wonderful.

00:16:07.040 --> 00:16:08.630
Behold!

00:16:13.300 --> 00:16:14.180
What's that?

00:16:14.760 --> 00:16:18.430
It's highly mobile,
and it's powered by the Song of Wind

00:16:18.510 --> 00:16:19.970
from the Echo Device.

00:16:20.350 --> 00:16:23.560
And it's easier to control than a horse!

00:16:24.690 --> 00:16:25.520
It's an airship!

00:16:26.310 --> 00:16:27.400
It's amazing!

00:16:28.020 --> 00:16:29.860
With this, we can rule the sky!

00:16:30.110 --> 00:16:32.990
This is Dr. Weissen at his best!

00:16:33.400 --> 00:16:36.200
Brave hero, fly to the Capital!

00:16:37.740 --> 00:16:39.910
This is so cool!

00:16:43.330 --> 00:16:44.750
We did it.

00:16:44.830 --> 00:16:47.500
The practice paid off!

00:16:48.040 --> 00:16:50.840
Okay. Leave Bazra
and the Capital Army to me.

00:16:51.300 --> 00:16:52.510
I'll stop them.

00:16:58.720 --> 00:17:00.470
It's almost the Star Song Festival.

00:17:01.270 --> 00:17:02.100
Yeah.

00:17:02.930 --> 00:17:04.600
I wish I could sing forever.

00:17:07.190 --> 00:17:09.610
I wish I could sing with everyone forever.

00:17:10.900 --> 00:17:11.780
Yeah.

00:17:14.950 --> 00:17:17.070
Let's stop the Song of Mortality.

00:17:17.660 --> 00:17:19.620
I wonder what it sounds like.

00:17:20.120 --> 00:17:20.950
Me too.

00:17:22.450 --> 00:17:23.330
Let me see.

00:17:27.000 --> 00:17:28.880
It's burnt in a few places.

00:17:30.710 --> 00:17:33.630
<i>A song that awakens</i>

00:17:33.710 --> 00:17:36.880
<i>And calls...</i>

00:17:36.970 --> 00:17:38.840
Huh? Isn't this--?

00:17:39.340 --> 00:17:42.680
<i>People repeat the song</i>

00:17:42.770 --> 00:17:45.520
<i>In their hearts</i>

00:17:47.640 --> 00:17:48.810
The Song of Healing?

00:17:50.190 --> 00:17:53.230
Why did you give us
the wrong Graphic notation, Al?

00:17:53.980 --> 00:17:55.820
No, that should be the right one.

00:17:56.400 --> 00:17:58.660
That's not the Song of Mortality.

00:17:58.740 --> 00:18:00.070
He's useless.

00:18:00.410 --> 00:18:01.280
Wimpyglasses.

00:18:01.370 --> 00:18:04.790
You didn't have to say that!
Who called me "wimpyglasses"?

00:18:05.830 --> 00:18:06.870
How bold of you!

00:18:08.290 --> 00:18:11.040
Hey. How do you read this?

00:18:11.460 --> 00:18:14.340
Do you see the patterns and characters
from the continent?

00:18:14.760 --> 00:18:16.130
These white things?

00:18:16.590 --> 00:18:19.220
White? What are you looking at?

00:18:19.640 --> 00:18:21.300
They're written in black ink.

00:18:21.640 --> 00:18:22.470
See?

00:18:25.600 --> 00:18:29.650
She tried to sing the Song of Mortality,
but it ended up as the Song of Healing.

00:18:30.020 --> 00:18:31.770
What are you mumbling about?

00:18:32.190 --> 00:18:34.110
He's making excuses.

00:18:34.190 --> 00:18:35.230
No, I'm not.

00:18:36.190 --> 00:18:39.110
I don't know how she read it wrong, but...

00:18:40.200 --> 00:18:43.830
she tried to sing the Song of Mortality,
but it ended up as the Song of Healing.

00:18:44.740 --> 00:18:47.080
There must be a reason!

00:18:47.750 --> 00:18:48.620
Al...

00:18:51.790 --> 00:18:52.750
If tomorrow comes,

00:18:53.670 --> 00:18:56.760
then that's the proof that we won!

00:18:58.170 --> 00:19:00.680
But if we lose, then tomorrow...

00:19:01.220 --> 00:19:02.590
will never come again.

00:19:03.180 --> 00:19:05.060
Today will be our last day.

00:19:05.970 --> 00:19:08.310
-Do you want to see the morning sun?
-Yeah!

00:19:08.390 --> 00:19:10.600
-Do you want to drink good alcohol?
-Yeah!

00:19:10.690 --> 00:19:12.690
Do you want to see your families' smiles?

00:19:15.020 --> 00:19:18.320
My friends! Let us meet again tomorrow!

00:19:20.110 --> 00:19:23.700
Leader! I think
this battle will go down in history.

00:19:24.160 --> 00:19:26.910
Of course. You're all heroes!

00:19:27.290 --> 00:19:29.870
Yeah. Then we need a name
befitting of heroes.

00:19:30.540 --> 00:19:32.040
What's our name?

00:19:32.580 --> 00:19:33.960
-Leader!
-Leader!

00:19:34.540 --> 00:19:35.960
Leader!

00:19:37.210 --> 00:19:40.300
From now on,
we shall be called the Lions Air Force!

00:19:41.010 --> 00:19:43.640
We'll fly through the sky
and take back the Capital!

00:19:46.680 --> 00:19:48.430
<i>The Lions Air Force!</i>

00:19:48.520 --> 00:19:49.980
<i>The Lions Air Force!</i>

00:19:50.230 --> 00:19:53.600
<i>-The Lions Air Force!</i>
-That's a cool name. The Lions Air Force.

00:19:59.690 --> 00:20:01.490
Well, let's go, too!

00:20:23.970 --> 00:20:25.550
Be careful out there.

00:20:25.890 --> 00:20:26.720
-Okay!
-Okay!

00:20:27.470 --> 00:20:29.470
Come back, no matter what.

00:20:30.270 --> 00:20:31.230
I promise.

00:20:35.850 --> 00:20:37.730
<i>Is that true?</i>

00:20:41.190 --> 00:20:42.240
Rin...

00:20:42.950 --> 00:20:44.150
You're...

00:20:46.240 --> 00:20:48.910
<i>Songs come to an end eventually.</i>

00:20:50.290 --> 00:20:52.540
<i>When the song reaches the person's heart,</i>

00:20:53.370 --> 00:20:55.460
<i>that's when it finishes its role...</i>

00:20:56.460 --> 00:20:57.790
<i>and disappears.</i>

00:20:59.090 --> 00:20:59.920
I...

00:21:00.960 --> 00:21:03.010
am a song that was sung for Finis.

00:21:04.760 --> 00:21:06.840
That means I'll probably...

00:21:08.930 --> 00:21:11.060
When that happens, I...

00:21:14.480 --> 00:21:15.310
Rin...

00:21:18.560 --> 00:21:19.650
But I'm fine.

00:21:20.360 --> 00:21:21.360
You know...

00:21:22.440 --> 00:21:23.990
when that happens,

00:21:25.200 --> 00:21:26.860
I'll probably be able...

00:21:28.070 --> 00:21:29.280
to save everyone I love.

00:21:44.800 --> 00:21:45.630
Are you ready?

00:21:46.760 --> 00:21:47.680
Prepare to launch!

00:22:03.610 --> 00:22:06.150
Let's go! We're headed to the Capital!

00:22:13.410 --> 00:22:14.290
Talgia...

00:22:15.250 --> 00:22:16.160
Please...

00:22:17.160 --> 00:22:19.080
<i>Please watch over her.</i>
